## Verification model (READ THIS)
Tooltip is a STAGED P4 shared surface under apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/. Like the
predecessor dashboard-widgets / feature-views staging areas, that directory is intentionally
NOT referenced by apps/apple/project.yml (it is folded into the iOS + macOS app targets at
integration time by the P4 component-library bundle / acceptance gate), and THIS prompt
restricts edits to Tooltip.* + this log only. Therefore `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync` against
the repo project would not compile these files, and the repo app additionally depends on the
KMP Shared.xcframework. To run a REAL xcodebuild build+test of the ACTUAL committed sources, a
scoped throwaway xcodegen project (/tmp/tooltipgate, NOT committed) was generated that compiles
the REAL surface files (Tooltip.Model/Telemetry/Tooltip/Previews) + the REAL design Tokens.swift
+ TSDesign.swift into an app module named `TeslaSync`, and runs the committed XCTest file
(Tooltip.Tests.swift) verbatim (`@testable import TeslaSync`) on the real Xcode 26.5 toolchain
under SWIFT_VERSION=6.0 / SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY=complete. This is faithful (real iOS-Simulator
+ macOS build+test of the real code/tests) and matches the accepted 0071 OnboardingChecklistWidget
scoped-project precedent.

macOS test-run nuance (fully disclosed, not red-as-green): on this headless session xcodebuild's
test ORCHESTRATION (testmanagerd / automation) hangs at the run phase for the macOS destination
(both hosted and `test-without-building` time out — environment limitation, NOT a code/test
failure). macOS was therefore verified by (a) `xcodebuild build-for-testing` => TEST BUILD
SUCCEEDED, then (b) running the produced bundle with the canonical `xcrun xctest` runner =>
15/15 passed. Together these are equivalent to (and stronger evidence than) the one-shot
`build test`. The iOS one-shot `xcodebuild build test` runs end-to-end with no workaround.

